# Common carotid artery flow-rate waveform: archetypal ensemble of 3560 cycles
# (Holdsworth et al. 1999, Physiol. Meas. 20:219-240), reconstructed here:
#  - Vpeak(t): the vector path of the cubic-spline curve of their figure 7(a),
#    extracted from the PDF and calibrated on the table-2 feature points
#    (residuals < 0.15 pt); period T_RR = 0.917 s, closed periodically;
#  - Vmean(t) from Vpeak(t) by their appendix eq. (A5), Womersley flow in a rigid
#    tube, D = 6.3 mm, nu = 3.5e-6 m^2/s, with tau_k = alpha_k i^{3/2}
#    (the e^{+ik w t} convention; the i^{-3/2} printed in (A5) gives negative
#    diastolic flow and does not reproduce their table 4);
#  - Q = Vmean pi D^2/4.
# Check against their table 4 (ml/s, ours/theirs): mean 6.11/6.0, Q0 3.95/4.0,
# QMIN 2.85/2.4, QA_MAX 12.44/12.3, QMAX 23.92/23.6, QHM 14.32/15.4, QDN 0.38/0.4.
# Peak/mean = 3.93. The driver keeps only the shape Q/mean; the period is set by Wo.
# columns: t (s)   Q (ml/s)
